# UI default — Carcará TUI

For **every** new or redesigned interactive flow, read `design-system/carcara/MASTER.md` and the playbook UI notes **before** coding.

1. Menus: **Zenity** `--list` (same pattern as `menuGeral.sh` / `menuSof.sh`).
2. Progress / short notices: **Yad** with shared `$configYad` / `$configYadB` from `config.sh`.
3. Keep window sizes readable (~330–500px width); center dialogs; short timeouts only for non-blocking notices.
4. One job per menu level; “Voltar” / “Sair” always available.
5. Do not introduce Electron or HTML installers for Carcará menus.
6. Prefer Portuguese UI labels consistent with existing menus unless localizing the whole app.
7. Keyboard: Zenity lists must work with Enter/Esc; never rely on hover-only affordances.
8. Progress dialogs must not hide apt errors — surface non-zero exits after the pulse.

Labeled primary actions may map to verbs (“Atualizar”, “Instalar”, “Limpar”, “Corrigir”) — see `design-system/carcara/MASTER.md`.
